  "pa_simulator": {
    "_comment_kbb": "FITTED K/BB model. The simulator predicted strikeouts from `contact_rate`, a per-swing whiff PROXY -- because StatcastProfile.k_rate was NEVER POPULATED (Savant's pull filters to batted balls; a strikeout is not one). MEASURED: sd = 0.0000 across 270 hitters. And league.contact_rate (0.7550) is the average over ALL batters while the model runs on STARTING LINEUPS (0.8178), so H_contact centres on +0.52 and k_hitter_contact (-1.05) turns that into -0.55 logits for EVERY hitter. A league-average starter produced K = 0.1365 against a realized 0.2198; the K floor then bound on 46.3% of the slate, hiding it; bip_prob was inflated 9.9% -- which carried 91.7% of the model's ENTIRE hits excess. The fitted model uses the hitter's OWN season/recent K and BB rates, which were ALREADY being fetched on every slate and handed only to the GBM. Coefficients are loaded only from the hash-bound artifact generated by scripts/fit_k_bb_final.py. Its complete fit/validation universe ends 2025-09-28; out-of-sample gains are +818.9 logL (K) and +308.9 (BB) over a constant. The PITCHER IS IN THE FIT, not added on top. ABSENT -> the simulator is BYTE-IDENTICAL to pre-fix.",
    "kbb_artifact_path": "data/learning/k_bb_pre2026.json",
    "kbb_artifact_sha256": "a6448d39d9ce1f0666b9656e848e10ac5ab2c9518a0bbff8eadeb753c2d08cc1",
    "use_fitted_kbb": true
  },
